#: ../../locations.md:30
msgid "Remix with URL parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:32
msgid "Using Remix with URL parameters will load the tool in the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:34
msgid "Remix URL parameters follow these conventions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:36
msgid "**`?#param=value`**: a query string (`?`) immediately followed by a hash fragment (`#`). `value` can be a plugin name, a comma-separated list of plugin names, a boolean (`true`/`false`), a theme name, a base64-encoded string, or a compiler version string. Used to activate or deactivate plugins, set a theme, minimize panels, load a base64-encoded file, and set a specific compiler build version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:37
msgid "**`#param=value`**: a hash fragment only, with no preceding query string. `value` can be a URL, an Ethereum address, a boolean, or a language name. Used to load a file via URL, load a verified contract from Etherscan, enable auto-compile, select the compiler language, and load a custom compiler from a URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:38
msgid "**`?param=value`**: a plain query string with no hash fragment. `value` is a Gist ID. Used to load a GitHub Gist into the File Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:39
msgid "**`//`**: a double slash delimiter used within `call` and `calls` values to separate a plugin's name, function, and arguments (e.g. `fileManager//open//contracts/3_Ballot.sol`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../locations.md:40
msgid "**`///`**: a triple slash delimiter used within `calls` to separate multiple plugin API calls from one another."
msgstr ""

